Fixed. In `ObservableSwitchMap$SwitchMapInnerObserver.onNext` (src/main/java/io/reactivex/rxjava3/internal/operators/observable/ObservableSwitchMap.java:239), the inner observer can be cancelled (e.g., the chain gets disposed while the inner source is still being subscribed), so `onSubscribe` never assigns `queue`, and the source's synchronous `onNext` then NPEs at `queue.offer(t)`.

The fix reads `queue` into a local and only offers/drains when it's non-null (matching the upstream RxJava fix for this issue):

```java
public void onNext(R t) {
    SimpleQueue<R> q = queue;
    if (index == parent.unique && q != null) {
        if (t != null) {
            q.offer(t);
        }
        drain();
    }
}
```

Verified with a standalone repro that NPEs before the fix and passes after, plus the SwitchMap TCK and mixed `switchMap*` tests pass.
